  "analysis": "Inclusion is the bottleneck: recall 0.22, 154 misses, mostly small (median 36px) and low-contrast faint smudges/elongated marks; round-1 tiny pastes (0.3-1.0, prefer_small) clearly did not help, so I shift to larger, learnable pastes and include the faint sources (287, 150, 11). Patches are decent (0.67) with small/low-contrast misses; keep the small-bias approach with a slightly higher floor. Scratches miss thin bright high-contrast lines (high-contrast recall only 0.33) plus faint thin lines; round-1 used all sources, so I now restrict to bright/faint thin-line sources matching the misses.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 25, "patches": 12, "scratches": 13},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.6, "scale_max": 1.4, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.0, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.2, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [100, 104, 106, 107, 112, 125, 134, 179, 180, 181, 182, 184, 185, 187, 191, 192, 200, 201, 203, 257, 258, 259, 291, 299, 41, 52, 53, 59, 60, 61, 63, 64, 98, 99]}
  },
  "rationale": "Round 1's tiny inclusion pastes failed (recall still 0.22), so inclusion gets the largest share (25) with a learnable 0.6-1.4 scale, uniform weighting, and all sources including the faint low-contrast ones (287/150/11) to better match the faint missed marks. Patches (12) keep the small-bias that correlates with their 0.67 recall, just with a higher scale floor. Scratches (13) now copy only thin bright/faint line sources to target the missed high-contrast thin lines that round 1's all-source mix under-served. Totals 50; all headroom/cap/span/overlap constraints satisfied."
}

